  "description": "North garden: \r1 x London plane (T1): Reduce longest branches projecting east by up to 3m in length, to suitable branch junctions to recreate a flowing canopy outline. \r1 x London plane (T2):   Reduce the crown to  0.5m below the existing reduction points in the crown.\r1 x London plane (T3): Re-pollard.  Retain selected shortened furnishing growth at cut points \r1 x London plane (T5): Reduce longest branches projecting east by up to 3m in length, to suitable branch junctions to recreate a flowing canopy outline. \r1 x lime (T7 ): Reduce crown by 2-3 metres. Remove epicormic growth and lift low canopy to 3 metres from ground level.\r1 x London plane (T8): Reduce crown to previous most recent reduction points. \r1 x lime (T11): Reduce dead limb to just above union with main stem in order to avoid cutting into live wood.  Remove epicormic growth to 3m from ground level. \r1 x lime (T14): Remove epicormic growth from base and trunk. \r1 x tree of heaven (T16): Lift low canopy to 4 metres from ground level.\r1 x sycamore (T18): Fell and treat stump.",
